          "previewAudio": "https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0051/8845/2401/files/chrysanthemum.mp3",
          "description": "Chrysanthemum thinks her name is absolutely perfect—until her first day of school. \"You're named after a flower!\" teases Victoria. \"Let's smell her,\" says Jo. Chrysanthemum wilts. What will it take to make her blossom again?\n\nThis is an ideal break-the-ice audiobook for the first week of school. It get children thinking about and bonding with their own names and the names of everyone else in the class, and it's the perfect vehicle for starting a discussion about treating classmates with tolerance, kindness, and compassion.",
